# The number in the next sentence is the SUM OF THE THREE COUNTERS printed just above, and
# never a literal. It was a literal `26`, correct on the day it was written and false from
# the commit that added S14/S15/S16 without touching it — so from 2026-08-30 to 2026-09-04
# the tool told every user it had run 26 checks while running 29, on the one sentence they
# read to size what was covered. Nothing was ignorant of the right number: the
# line directly above printed 0+23+6, and the suite asserted 29 twice in the same run. The
# two numbers simply never met. A count the product PRINTS is recomputed at print time
